{
  "version": 1,
  "operation": "SdpaBackward",
  "description": "SDPA backward with Philox dropout (a probability, an INT64 seed and an INT64 offset as device tensors with exact `values` fills, so metadata format_version 2) over hipkernel:flydsl_sdpa_bwd_split (COVERAGE.md 9.1 DR-1 to DR-6). No reference reproduces an engine's random stream, but SEM-015 pins the mask bits (Philox4x32-10 keyed by the seed, counter offset + ((b * Hq + h) * Sq + i) * ceil(Skv / 4) + j / 4, kept iff the word at j % 4 read as int32 exceeds int32(f32(p - 0.5) * 2^32)), so the harness draws the keep mask itself (harness/input-init/PhiloxDropout.hpp): it derives O and the LSE from the forward over that mask with the scale 1 / (1 - p), and grades the engine against the explicit-mask backward gradient (scale 1 / (1 - p), scale inverse 1 - p), which is the exact gradient. The engine's gradient is correct only when its regenerated mask is that mask, so a mismatch in the mask bits shows as a WRONG over every probability. Seeds include negative and large values, offsets past 2^32 (the counter's high word). Masks none, causal (both alignments, MW-11 accepts dropout with bottom-right) and windows. The seed and offset tensors are named z_seed and z_offset so their canonical uids (sorted name, bundle_utils.canonical_uid_map_by_name) are 10 and 9.",
